{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "sint-02-finding-principal-rate-time-amount",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Finding Principal, Rate, Time, and Amount",
    "description": "Reverse the simple-interest relationship confidently to recover whichever quantity is missing.",
    "teachingApproach": "Use the same simple-interest model, but turn it around one variable at a time. Each worked example should show the missing quantity as the only unknown, followed immediately by a fresh question that looks nearly the same. Build toward amount-based and month-based reverse problems so learners learn to recognise the structure, not memorise four unrelated formulas.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 30,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 22, Simple Interest (printed pp. 641–662). Approved scope: Teach the four-way reversal of S.I. = PRT/100: finding principal, rate, time, and amount. Include amount-first questions where S.I. must first be found as A−P, growth-factor questions A=P(1+RT/100), reverse questions with months, and proportional shortcuts when only rate changes. Emphasise identifying the missing quantity before calculating and checking the result forward in the original relation."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Finding Principal, Rate, Time, and Amount\n\nReverse the simple-interest relationship confidently to recover whichever quantity is missing.\n\nWe will build the idea with small numbers first, then move into the exam-style patterns from the chapter.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The formula can run backwards. If S.I., rate, and time are known, the principal is the one missing factor.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "If S.I. = ₹1200 at 8% for 3 years, then P = 1200 × 100 ÷ (8 × 3) = ₹5000.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
